## Why it is research, not a dashboard

- **Measurement before claims.** The feed is irregular (a {{ data.clock_ms }} ms clock, gaps of up to {{ data.interval_max_s }} s in the pilot session, about {{ data.metres_between_samples_300 }} m between
  samples at 300 km/h, nothing faster than {{ data.nyquist_hz }} Hz visible). Every feature was tested on synthetic laps with a
  known truth first. For example, "the first sample with the brake on" is {{ measure.onset_naive_bias_m }} m late on average; the chosen
  estimator has {{ measure.onset_chosen_rmse_m }} m error. A causal moving average shifts the middle of a braking event by {{ measure.ma5_mid_shift_m }} m, so events are
  located on raw samples.
- **Alignment.** Laps are placed on one track coordinate by a complementary filter (integrated speed + car position),
  with {{ measure.alignment_m }} m along-track error.
- **No leakage, honest baselines.** Identification is always leave-one-weekend-out and is compared with lap time,
  simple lap statistics and shuffled labels (which score {{ h3.final.shuffled }}, as they should).
- **A frozen test set.** 2025 was refused by the code until the preregistration was committed, then run once. A
  crash before any result, and a team changer missing from the plan, are both reported as deviations.

## Run it

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e .
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest          # all tests, on synthetic data (also run by GitHub Actions)
.venv\Scripts\python.exe run.py             # the web app: http://127.0.0.1:5000
```

The Overview, Corner lab and Driver vs car pages work from the committed results. The Lap compare page also needs
the raw lap samples, which are not in the repository: `experiments/08_download_openf1.py` and
`experiments/09_build_dataset.py` download and rebuild them from OpenF1 (about an hour, rate-limited).

## Repository map

| Folder | What |
|---|---|
| `src/apextrace/` | the package: data loading, quality checks, filters, alignment, events, features, statistics, identification, signatures |
| `experiments/` | numbered scripts `00`–`17`; every number and figure comes from one of them |
| `results/` | small outputs (JSON, CSV, figures); `results/final/` holds the frozen 2025 test |
| `app/` | the web app (Flask, vanilla JavaScript, D3) |
| `tests/` | pytest tests on synthetic signals; they never download F1 data |
| `docs/` | report, preregistration, deviations, research log, decisions, data report, related work |
| `learn/` | a guide to every part of the project, chapter by chapter, with viva questions |

## Limitations

Qualifying laps only; a public feed at about {{ data.rate_hz }} Hz with an on/off brake signal (no pressure); position data
too coarse to see racing lines; five team changers in the final test, so H4 could only pass if all five agreed. The
report lists these and more.

